# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Install-time / build artifacts — never commit.
#
# test/install.mjs implements the hot-reload scheme described in README: it
# publishes the implementation as a freshly named `lib/releases/impl-<build>.js`
# inside the *installed* copy and rewrites `lib/current-build.txt` to point at
# it. Those paths are per-machine state regenerated on every install, so
# committing them would pin one machine's stale build (and its timestamped build
# id) into the repository. The workspace copy of `lib/index.js` is the canonical
# source and IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
lib/releases/
lib/current-build.txt

# Common noise
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Transient desktop screenshot written by docs/capture.ps1.
# NOTE: docs/toast-verified.png and docs/toast-alerts.png are real verification
# screenshots and are intentionally tracked.
docs/capture.png
